<title>SWEDEN: MoDo posts 44 pct fall in 1996 profit.</title>
<headline>MoDo posts 44 pct fall in 1996 profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish forestry company MoDo posts its earnings for the 12 months ending December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		  2,919 vs   5,216</p>
<p> Sales					20,115 vs  22,319</p>
<p> Proposed dividend (SKR)		  9.00 vs   8.50</p>
<p> Operating costs			  15,601 vs  15,692</p>
<p> Non-recurring items			  11 vs     282</p>
<p> Associate interests			   4 vs	73</p>
<p> Depreciation				1,239 vs   1,151</p>
<p> Operating profit			  3,290 vs   5,831</p>
<p> Net financial items	     CHARGE  371 vs     615 CHARGE</p>
<p> Tax					     940 vs   1,545</p>
<p> Net profit				  1,979 vs   3,671</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuters poll found analysts were expectintg MoDo to post a profit after financial items of 3.06 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
